        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "So I've had this experience a few times now.\r\n\r\nI learned that I was playing something incorrectly in the tabletop version of the game because of what happens in the video game. Has this happened to anyone else?\r\n\r\nHere's what I discovered today.\r\n1. Wager Master's \"Breaking the Rules\" causes each player to draw TWO cards at the End of Turn, presumably because you haven't played a card or used a power that turn. Even though you probably will.\r\n2. Also dealing with Breaking the Rules: If a card effect, such as Scholar's \"Know When to Hold Fast\" or Nightmist's \"Mist-Fueled Recovery,\" causes you to immediately end your turn, you get to immediately have a second turn!\r\n\r\nAs a side-note Darkwatch Nightmist + Breaking the Rules = stack your own deck.",
